//[user 2026-08-31] the 17 allied panic screams behind coop_av_us_panic
//(maps/m3l1a/coopified.scr::coop_beachPanic). Cached at load so the CS_SOUNDS configstrings
//are allocated here rather than broadcast mid-firefight - m3l3_precache.scr:19 does the same.
//[bug-2341] THE WRECKAGE FIELD'S MODELS, LOADED AT MAP LOAD RATHER THAN IN PLAY.
//
//coop_beachWreckage spawns ~125 props from a thread AFTER init, and none of these 29 models had ever
//been referenced by this map - so the first spawn of each one loaded a TIKI, its skeleton and its
//shaders live. Two things came of that on the first headless boot: a 4674 msec hitch, and an
//intermittent 0xC0000005 whose faulting module was ntdll rather than any game code. A fault inside
//ntdll is the signature of heap damage tripped over later by an unrelated free, and runtime TIKI
//loading is precisely where this project has produced that before - bug-2292 was a skeletor cache
//overrun sized by a constant that only coincidentally matched the entity pool.
//
//Caching them here moves every one of those loads into the map load, where the engine expects them,
//and the hitch goes with it. bh_water_hard and water_trail_bubble were already cached by this file,
//which is why the underwater rounds needed nothing.
//=========================================================================
cache models/static/af_p_lifepreserver.tik
cache models/animate/gasmask.tik
cache models/static/static_m1_garand.tik
cache models/static/static_thompsonsmg.tik
cache models/static/body_us01.tik
cache models/static/body_us02.tik
cache models/static/body_us03.tik
cache models/static/body_us04.tik
cache models/static/body_us05.tik
cache models/static/body_us06.tik
cache models/coop_build/box_crate_30cal.tik
cache models/static/static_bangalore.tik
cache models/static/af_p_stretcher.tik
cache models/static/cot.tik
cache models/items/papers.tik
cache models/static/typewriter.tik

